msgid "plugins.importexport.csv.form.zipHelp"
msgstr "<b>Monographs:</b> Upload a ZIP file built in one of two simple ways:<br><br><b>Option 1 — Everything together:</b> Put your CSV file and all its assets (PDFs, images, and other files) side by side at the top level of the ZIP.<br><br><b>Option 2 — Everything in one folder:</b> Put your CSV file and all its assets inside a single folder, then ZIP that folder. The plugin finds the folder automatically.<br><br>In both cases, the file path you write in each CSV column must match where the file actually sits in the ZIP. If a file is inside a subfolder, use its relative path (e.g., <em>galleys/monograph.pdf</em>). Files named <em>invalid_*.csv</em> are reserved for error output and are skipped during import."

msgid "plugins.importexport.csv.form.examplesHelp"
msgstr "<b>Need an example?</b> You can view and download ready-to-use sample CSV files here: <a href=\"https://github.com/Godoy0722/omp_csv_importexport/tree/stable-3_5_0/examples/monographs\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">CSV examples</a>."

msgid "plugins.importexport.csv.form.userImportHelp"
msgstr "<b>Users:</b> Import user accounts with roles. Your CSV file should include columns such as pressPath, firstname, lastname, email, roles, and optional fields like affiliation, country, username, tempPassword, reviewInterests, and orcid. Enable the welcome email option to automatically notify new users of their account creation."

msgid "plugins.importexport.csv.form.usersExamplesHelp"
msgstr "<b>Need an example?</b> You can view and download ready-to-use sample user CSV files here: <a href=\"https://github.com/Godoy0722/ops_csv_importexport/tree/stable-3_5_0/examples/users\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">CSV examples for users</a>."

