msgid "plugins.importexport.csv.results.intro.monographs"
msgstr "This is the result of importing <b>monographs</b>. Every row of your CSV files was processed: rows that succeeded were saved to the press, and any that failed are listed further down together with the reason they could not be imported."

msgid "plugins.importexport.csv.results.intro.monographs.dryMode"
msgstr "This is a <b>Data Validation</b> for <b>monographs</b> — nothing was saved to the press. The summary below is a preview of what a real import would do: it shows which rows would be created and which would fail, along with the reason for each failure. When you are happy with the result, disable <b>Data Validation</b> and import again to apply the changes."

msgid "plugins.importexport.csv.results.intro.users"
msgstr "This is the result of importing <b>users</b>. Every row of your CSV files was processed: rows that succeeded were created as user accounts, and any that failed are listed further down together with the reason they could not be imported."

msgid "plugins.importexport.csv.results.legend"
msgstr "The counters below show the totals for this run, followed by a per-file breakdown. Each failed row is listed with its row number and the reason it failed, so you can fix it in the CSV and import again."

msgid "plugins.importexport.csv.results.invalidFilesHint"
msgstr "For every CSV that had failed rows, a downloadable copy named <b>invalid_&lt;your-file&gt;.csv</b> is generated containing only those failed rows. Click the file name shown below each error table to download it, fix the rows, and import again."

